    "q-162404": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162404",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Find the radius of curvature for the curve $r(t)=({t}^{2}-1)\\,i+(1-t)\\,j$ at $t=\\frac{1}{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The curvature $κ(t)$ of a plane curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{|{x}^{′}(t){y}^{″}(t)-{y}^{′}(t){x}^{″}(t)|}{([{x}^{′}(t)]^{2}+[{y}^{′}(t)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nThe radius of curvature $R$ is defined as\n$R(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}.$\n\nAlong our curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2}-1,\\,y(t)=1-t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the derivatives of the components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =2t,\\, & {y}^{′}(t) & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =2,\\, & {y}^{″}(t) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the curvature, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{|2t\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 2|}{{((2t)^{2}+(-1)^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{(4{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=\\frac{1}{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\frac{2}{{(4{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{(1+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the radius of curvature at $t=\\frac{1}{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\frac{1}{κ(\\frac{1}{2})}=\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-162404-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\sqrt{2}",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"83\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msqrt><mjx-sqrt><mjx-surd><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c221A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-surd><mjx-box style=\"padding-top: 0.174em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-box></mjx-sqrt></mjx-msqrt></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
